# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# WHY: this repository is developed on a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites tracked text files to CRLF on checkout.
# A CRLF shell script does not run under WSL or Linux — bash reports
# "set: - : invalid option" and "$'\r': command not found", which points at
# nothing useful. scripts/run_tests.sh, the one command the README and
# onboarding doc tell a newcomer to run, was broken this way.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Terraform and CI configuration are read by Linux tooling for the same reason.
*.tf     text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
